      <h3 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-normal text-gray-900 mb-3">Pitfalls of DIY AI vs Professional Implementation</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">When considering AI implementation, SMEs in Nepal often face a crucial decision: should they attempt to develop AI solutions in-house (DIY) or seek professional services? Understanding the pros and cons of each approach can guide businesses toward successful AI adoption.

### DIY AI Implementation
<strong>Pros:</strong>
- Cost-effective for smaller projects, as businesses can leverage existing developer resources.
- Full control over the development process and the ability to customize solutions based on immediate needs.

<strong>Cons:</strong>
- May lack the expertise necessary to build effective AI solutions, leading to suboptimal performance.
- Increased risk of time and resource wastage if the project fails to meet business objectives.

### Professional AI Implementation
<strong>Pros:</strong>
- Access to specialized knowledge and resources, speeding up the development process and ensuring best practices.
- Greater capabilities for complex projects that require machine learning engineers or AI consultants.

<strong>Cons:</strong>
- Higher initial cost, which may not be feasible for all SMEs.
- Less direct control over the project, potentially creating misalignment in objectives.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mb-8 last:mb-0">
      <h3 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-normal text-gray-900 mb-3">Building vs Buying AI Solutions</h3>
      <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">Deciding whether to build or buy your AI solution is essential for your implementation strategy. This comparison can help you determine the best path based on your specific needs and resources.

### Build vs Buy
| Aspect                | Build                        | Buy                           |
|----------------------|------------------------------|-------------------------------|
| <strong>Cost</strong>             | Higher upfront investment, considering hiring and training costs | Subscription or licensing costs, lower initial investment |
| <strong>Time to Deployment</strong> | Longer, as development and testing take time | Quicker to implement since solutions are pre-built |
| <strong>Customization</strong>     | Highly customizable to specific needs | Limited customization, mainly suited for standard use cases |
| <strong>Maintenance</strong>      | Ongoing development and maintenance required | Vendor handles updates and support, which can ease the burden |
| <strong>Scalability</strong>      | Potentially easier to scale as per growth | May require upgrades or new purchases for scaling |

In general: SMEs are advised to opt for buying off-the-shelf solutions for standard use cases like chatbots and search functionalities, but consider building custom solutions for unique needs or competitive differentiation.</p>
